window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-41eff5c7a74dc9b5"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"turn-user-stories-into-ui-mocks\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"ui\">将用户故事转化为 UI 样稿</h1> <p>把产品反馈、问题讨论和设计背景转化为团队可讨论、可实现的样稿。</p> <p>使用 Codex 汇总 Slack、Linear 和 Google Drive 中的产品反馈，将信息整理为用户故事和约束条件，再用 ImageGen 生成 UI 样稿；确定方向后，将样稿实现为可运行的原型。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要把分散的反馈整理成某项功能视觉方向的产品团队。</li> <li>希望先根据结构化设计背景制作样稿的设计与工程团队。</li> <li>希望根据用户反馈快速迭代的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>从已获准访问的反馈频道和讨论串中查找用户故事、痛点、原话和待解决问题。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/linear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">linear（需联网）</a></td> <td>将功能请求、缺陷报告、标签、优先级和项目背景整理到样稿说明中。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>阅读包含产品反馈或设计要求的研究笔记、通话摘要、文档、表格和幻灯片。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/figma\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">figma（需联网）</a></td> <td>获取设计背景、截图和设计系统参考，避免样稿偏离产品既有的视觉语言。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$imagegen</code></td> <td>根据综合整理出的用户故事和设计约束生成 UI 样稿、不同方案及视觉参考。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-web-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>将选定的样稿转化为可运行的 Web 原型，并根据样稿验证实现效果。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>根据用户故事制作 UI 样稿</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请根据这份 [user story/set of user feedbacks]（用户故事/用户反馈集合），为解决相应问题的功能制作 UI 样稿，并参考以下来源：\n- @slack [channels or thread links]（频道或讨论串链接）\n- @linear [issue links, project, team, or view]（issue 链接、项目、团队或视图）\n- @google-drive [research notes, survey export, doc, sheet, or slide deck]（研究笔记、调查结果、文档、表格或幻灯片）\n\n制作时请遵循当前设计系统和现有 UI [provide Figma file or screenshot as reference]（提供 Figma 文件或截图作为参考）。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">简介</h2> <p>产品团队经常从不同来源收集反馈，例如 Slack 讨论串、Linear issue、Google Drive 文档或表格，以及客户通话笔记。有时，团队已经整理出了清晰的用户故事；有时，相关背景则散落在这些资料中。</p> <p>ChatGPT 可以汇总这些背景，并据此制作能够解决问题的功能 UI 样稿。确定方向后，Codex 可以在产品中实现它。</p> <p><a id=\"generate-visual-truth\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">生成可信的视觉方案</h2> <p>如果已经有清晰的用户故事，可以直接从它开始；如果还没有，可以先与 ChatGPT 讨论，从多个来源收集背景并综合整理为用户故事。</p> <p>然后，可以让 ChatGPT 使用图像生成功能创建几种 UI 方向。样稿应遵循产品的信息架构和设计系统约束。</p> <p>如果有帮助，也可以提供当前 UI 的截图或 Figma 文件作为参考。</p> <p>持续调整，直到你对样稿满意。改动范围越明确，Codex 越有可能生成可直接实现的样稿。</p> <p><a id=\"move-from-mock-to-prototype\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">从样稿走向原型</h2> <p>选定希望 Codex 实现的最终样稿图片。切换到 Codex，开启新对话，并重新附上图片，不要直接在 ChatGPT 对话中继续。然后让 Codex 实现样稿；如果要构建 Web 应用，可以选择使用 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build Web Apps plugin（需联网）</a>，把样稿变成可运行的原型：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use this image as a reference and implement this feature in this repository. Use this chat's context to help you implement it with the right constraints. Minimize the creation of new components: explore the codebase and reuse existing components and design system when possible.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">以这张图片为参考，在这个代码仓库中实现该功能。利用这个聊天的上下文，帮助你在正确的约束下完成实现。尽量减少新组件的创建：先探索代码库，并尽可能复用现有组件和设计系统。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"turn-user-stories-into-ui-mocks\">Turn user stories into UI mocks</h1> <p>Convert product feedback, issue threads, and design context into mockups your team can react to and implement.</p> <p>Use Codex to gather product feedback from Slack, Linear, Google Drive, normalize it into user stories and constraints, then generate UI mockups with ImageGen. When the direction is chosen, turn the mock into a working prototype.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Product teams turning scattered feedback into a visual direction for a feature.</li> <li>Design and engineering teams that want mockups grounded in source material before building.</li> <li>Teams who want to iterate fast based on user feedback.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Search approved feedback channels and threads for user stories, pain points, quotes, and open questions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/linear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">linear (online)</a></td> <td>Pull feature requests, bug reports, labels, priorities, and project context into the mock brief.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read research notes, call summaries, docs, sheets, and slides that contain product feedback or design requirements.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/figma\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">figma (online)</a></td> <td>Fetch design context, screenshots, and design-system references so mocks do not drift away from the product's visual language.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$imagegen</code></td> <td>Generate UI mockups, variations, and visual truth from the synthesized stories and design constraints.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-web-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Turn the selected mock into a working web prototype and verify the implementation against the mock.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Create Mocks from User Stories</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this [user story/set of user feedbacks] into a UI mock for a feature that would solve the problem, using these sources as context:\n- @slack [channels or thread links]\n- @linear [issue links, project, team, or view]\n- @google-drive [research notes, survey export, doc, sheet, or slide deck]\n\nDo that while respecting the current design system and existing UI [provide Figma file or screenshot as reference].\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>Product teams often collect feedback from various sources, such as Slack threads, Linear issues, Google Drive docs or sheets, or customer-call notes. Sometimes, they have clear user stories illustrating a problem they want to solve, and sometimes, the context lives in those sources.</p> <p>ChatGPT can gather this context and turn it into a UI mock for a feature that would solve the problem. Once you validate the direction, Codex can implement it in the product.</p> <h2 id=\"generate-visual-truth\">Generate visual truth</h2> <p>If you have a clear user story, you can start with that. If not, you can have a discussion with ChatGPT first, gathering context from different sources and synthesizing it into a user story.</p> <p>Then, you can ask ChatGPT to use image generation to create a few mock directions. The mocks should preserve the product's information architecture and design-system constraints.</p> <p>If helpful, you can provide screenshots of the current UI or a Figma file as reference.</p> <p>Do this until you are satisfied with the mock. The more scoped the changes are, the more likely Codex is to generate a mock that can be implemented directly.</p> <h2 id=\"move-from-mock-to-prototype\">Move from mock to prototype</h2> <p>Use the final mock image that you want Codex to implement. Select Codex, start a new chat, and reattach the image rather than continuing the ChatGPT chat directly. Then ask Codex to implement the mock—optionally using the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build Web Apps plugin (online)</a> if you're building a web app—to turn it into a working prototype:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use this image as a reference and implement this feature in this repository. Use this chat's context to help you implement it with the right constraints. Minimize the creation of new components: explore the codebase and reuse existing components and design system when possible.\n</code></pre>"};
